// REJECTS: Unexpected token 'runtimeComponents'. Valid alternatives: ['query', 'mapping', 'runtime']
//
// `runtimeComponents` is an ExecutionEnvironment keyword. It is legal in exactly one place --
// inside a singleExecEnv of an `ExecutionEnvironment` element -- and nowhere inside a
// Service's `execution: Single` block, whose only arms are query/mapping/runtime.
//
// Both elements live in the SAME section (###Service, `imports (service | execEnvs)* EOF`)
// and both spell their bodies with `mapping:` and `runtime:`, so a rewritten parser that
// keeps one shared "execution body" rule will accept this silently. The divergence never
// shows up as a failure: it shows up as a model legend-lite loads and legend-engine refuses.
###Service
Service fixture::neg::ComponentsInExecution
{
   pattern: '/fixture/neg/components';
   documentation: 'runtimeComponents belongs to an ExecutionEnvironment, not a Service execution';
   execution: Single
   {
      runtimeComponents:
      {
         class: fixture::neg::Person;
         binding: fixture::neg::PersonBinding;
         runtime: fixture::neg::Runtime;
      }
   }
}
